        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by the introduction of raw types in the code, which can lead to type safety issues and compilation errors. The lack of explicit type parameters in collections and generics can result in ClassCastExceptions at runtime and make the code harder to understand and maintain. The modifications aimed to replace raw types with specific types, particularly `EquivalentValue`, to ensure type safety and improve code clarity.

        Commit message:
        fixed some compilations issues introduced in
 70435f456d73b3ee2e555b8b4ec46df0b4411951 and added more type information  

        Patch:

 	public SimpleMethodInfoFlowAnalysis(UnitGraph g, InfoFlowAnalysis dfa, boolean ignoreNonRefTypeFlow)
